														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4750380">
									

<p>So YouTuber Tom Scott gave <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/qntm" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(571081); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=571081&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1597725077" alt="qntm" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=571081)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/qntm" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(571081); return false;">qntm</a></span> (author page here: <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/qntm-s-author-page">http://www.scpwiki.com/qntm-s-author-page</a>), and indirectly the SCP wiki, a shout-out in a video posted today: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hr03xF08qoU">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hr03xF08qoU</a> (&quot;Is The Most Northern Part Of Iceland Still There?&quot;)</p>
<p>Tom Scott actually has a bunch of videos in his Amazing Places series that make pretty great SCP fuel&#8212;here are my personal favorites:</p>
<ul>
<li>The Poison Garden of Alnwick: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jGo9gYypQc8">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jGo9gYypQc8</a></li>
<li>The Broken Building That Must Not Be Destroyed: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AtkmDmMzZO8">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AtkmDmMzZO8</a> (there's actually some comments about the title sounding like that of an SCP object)</li>
<li>The Lava Lamps That Help Keep The Internet Secure: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1cUUfMeOijg">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1cUUfMeOijg</a> (esoteric containment procedures, anyone?)</li>
<li>I Hit 3,000-Year-Old Art with a Hammer: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s6kNR8Mj0ZE">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s6kNR8Mj0ZE</a> (aka The White Horse, in Uffington)</li>
</ul>
<p>Does anyone else watch this series?</p>

