<blockquote>
<p>I don't feel like I have to pay quite as much attention as I do with the youtube stuff I normally watch (two-hour long deconstruction of the problems with an obscure web show, hour-long video on mid-1800s philosophy and politics etc.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Agreed&#8212;the Amazing Places videos are very readily approachable/digestible. Ditto for Things You Might Not Know. I like to have them playing in the background while I do chores like cleaning my fishtanks or watering my plant army.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I try not to get too excited about seeing the wiki and it's influence in the wild because it's to be expected given the amount of time the site has been around for and the number of members it's accumulated</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I still do double takes when I see SCP pop up in comment sections of seemingly totally unrelated YouTube videos. At any rate, it's nice to know that others in the community like watching the same material!</p>

